---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import PageIntro from "../components/PageIntro.astro";
import { href, source } from "../lib/links";
---

<Layout
    title="Research"
    description="Research question, methods and boundaries for network anomaly detection and traceability."
    section="Research"
>
    <PageIntro
        eyebrow="01 / Research"
        current="Research"
        title="Research with a clear boundary."
        description="The project investigates network-flow detection and the evidence needed to explain a security finding. Its target architecture extends beyond the capabilities currently present on main."
    />
    <div class="container section research-grid">
        <article class="prose">
            <h2 id="problem">The problem</h2><p>
                Labelled intrusion benchmarks make model comparison possible,
                but a high score on one dataset can reflect repeated flows or
                laboratory-specific patterns. A useful detection system also
                needs a traceable path from an observation to the evidence,
                without treating an IP address as proof of a person's identity.
            </p>
            <h2 id="objectives">Research objectives</h2><ol>
                <li>
                    Establish a reproducible baseline on verified
                    NF-UNSW-NB15-v3 bytes.
                </li><li>
                    Compare supervised classification with unsupervised anomaly
                    scores under explicit split and threshold rules.
                </li><li>
                    Audit shortcuts, equivalent feature vectors, false positives
                    and false negatives.
                </li><li>
                    Design behavioral correlation, explainable risk scoring and
                    evidence-linked incident timelines for a later system layer.
                </li>
            </ol>
            <h2 id="method">Method</h2><p>
                The published v3 CSV is verified by manifest and quality checks.
                A chronological, group-aware split with purge gaps assigns
                Train, Validation and Test before learned preprocessing. The
                baseline model contract keeps 47 ordered flow features and
                separates six trace metadata fields and the two targets.
                Train-only statistics are frozen for later partitions.
                Validation is used for model and threshold work; held-out Test
                claims require a separate, auditable evaluation.
            </p>
            <h2 id="contributions">Expected contributions</h2><p>
                The intended contribution is a transparent research pipeline:
                provenance and schema, reproducible preprocessing, comparable
                model protocols, diagnostic evaluation and a future traceable
                decision path. Only the first parts have repository evidence
                today. Risk scoring, incident correlation, secure storage and a
                user interface remain roadmap work.
            </p>
            <h2 id="limitations">Limits and next work</h2><p>
                The v3 package was published in 2025, while its observed flows
                are from early 2015. Near-perfect Validation scores cannot
                establish performance on current or external networks. The
                current record identifies TTL shortcuts and extensive
                feature-vector equivalence. Cross-dataset testing,
                Test-partition evaluation and operational security review are
                still needed.
            </p>
            <div class="callout">
                <strong>Interpretation rule</strong><br />Unknown-attack
                holdouts would test a defined experimental protocol; they would
                not prove zero-day detection in the real world.
            </div>
        </article>
        <aside class="source-rail" aria-label="Research sources">
            <span class="eyebrow">Source trail</span><a
                href={source("docs/PROBLEM_STATEMENT.md")}
                >Problem statement ↗</a
            ><a href={source("docs/METHODOLOGY.md")}>Methodology ↗</a><a
                href={source("docs/ROADMAP_FULL_SYSTEM.md")}
                >Full-system roadmap ↗</a
            ><a href={source("docs/NF_UNSW_NB15_V3_SPLIT_PROTOCOL.md")}
                >Split protocol ↗</a
            ><a href={href("docs/limitations/")}>Read limitations →</a>
        </aside>
    </div>
</Layout>
<style>
    .research-grid {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 250px;
        gap: 5rem;
    }
    .source-rail {
        align-self: start;
        position: sticky;
        top: 110px;
        border-left: 1px solid var(--line);
        padding-left: 1.5rem;
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 0.75rem;
    }
    .source-rail a {
        font-size: 0.85rem;
        color: var(--muted);
    }
    @media (max-width: 800px) {
        .research-grid {
            grid-template-columns: 1fr;
            gap: 2rem;
        }
        .source-rail {
            position: static;
        }
    }
</style>
